      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\n`save_sharded_state` serializes each worker's in-memory `state_dict()`, i.e. the\r\nweights *after* `process_weights_after_loading`. Some post-processing leaves a\r\nweight as a non-contiguous view with a widened row stride. On ROCm,\r\n`VLLM_ROCM_FP8_PADDING` (on by default) does exactly that with `F.pad(w, (0, n))[..., :-n]`.\r\n\r\nSaving such a model fails twice over:\r\n\r\n1. `ShardedStateLoader._filter_subtensors` computes a tensor's end address with\r\n   `tensor.view(-1)[-1]`, which raises on a strided view:\r\n   `RuntimeError: view size is not compatible with input tensor's size and stride`.\r\n2. Even past that, `safetensors.save_file` refuses non-contiguous tensors:\r\n   `ValueError: You are trying to save a non contiguous tensor`.\r\n\r\n## Test plan\r\n\r\n**1. FP8 model** `Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B-FP8`\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npython examples/features/sharded_state/save_sharded_state_offline.py \\\r\n    --model Qwen3-0.6B-FP8 --output /tmp/q3-fp8-sharded\r\n```\r\n- fails on main, passes here\r\n\r\nLoading that FP8 checkpoint back is a separate, pre-existing problem: it fails\r\nwith `Missing keys (...attn.q_scale, ...k_scale, ...v_scale, ...prob_scale)`\r\non main too, even with `VLLM_ROCM_FP8_PADDING=0`, because those attention\r\nscales are deleted in `process_weights_after_loading` and so never saved. It\r\nis out of scope here.\r\n\r\n**2. w4a16 model ** `Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B`:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npython examples/features/sharded_state/save_sharded_state_offline.py \\\r\n    --model Qwen3-0.6B --output /tmp/q3-sharded\r\npython examples/features/sharded_state/load_sharded_state_offline.py \\\r\n    --model /tmp/q3-sharded --load-format sharded_state \\\r\n    --prompt \"The capital of France is\" --max-tokens 32 --temperature 0\r\n```\r\n- fails on main, passes here\r\n\r\n## Not a duplicate\r\n\r\nNo duplicate PRs found.\r\n\r\n## AI assistance\r\n\r\nAI assistance was used for this PR. I reviewed every changed line, and ran the\r\ntests and the end-to-end round trip listed above.\r\n",
